<h2 id="when-to-use">When to use this pattern</h2>
<p>Use a page not found if someone is trying to view a page that does not exist. This happens if someone:</p>
<ul>
    <li>selects a link or button that takes them to a page that does not exist</li>
    <li>types or copies a web address for a page that does not exist</li>
    <li>types or copies a web address incorrectly</li>
</ul>
<p>Try to avoid having any broken links in your service by:</p>
<ul>
  <li>testing all links and buttons to make sure they work</li>
  <li>checking that all the web addresses in your service, including posters or letters, are correct</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="how-to-use">How to use this pattern</h2>
<p>The page should include:</p>
<ul>
    <li>"Page not found – service name – NHS" as the page title</li>
    <li>"Page not found" as the <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code></li>
    <li>options to navigate to the start page in a service or the home page in a website</li>
    <li>an <a href="#with-alternative-journey">alternative journey</a>, for users on a transactional service</li>
    <li><a href="#contact-information">contact information</a>, if it helps meet a user need</li>
</ul>

<p>If your users find it helpful, include a search option.</p>
<p>Do not ask the public to report broken links, unless you know that this meets a user need. On internal systems and services, users may expect to report issues.</p>

<p>The content should be clear and concise, not blame the user.</p>

<p>Do not use:</p>
<ul>
    <li>breadcrumbs</li>
    <li>technical jargon like "404" or "bad request"</li>
    <li>informal or humorous words like "oops"</li>
    <li>red text to warn people</li>
    <li>too many links</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="with-alternative-journey">Page not found with an alternative journey</h3>
<p>If your users are trying to complete a task, offer them an alternative way to do it. For example, another way to complete a form.</p>
<p>Consider the options with your clinical team.</p>
{{ designExample({
  group: "patterns",
  item: "page-not-found-page",
  type: "alternative-journey"
}) }}

<h4 id="contact-information">Contact information</h4>
<p>Include contact information if it meets a user need or helps them complete their task. For example, if someone wants to cancel an appointment.</p>
<p>Contact information should include all numbers and opening times or link to a specific page that includes numbers and opening times.</p>

{{ designExample({
  group: "patterns",
  item: "page-not-found-page",
  type: "with-contact-details"
}) }}

